b994798da63f/master/w_1600,c_limit/4812bce41c0608a288ca072e917553aa.jpg","line":120,"embedded":true},{"title":"*here*","target":"https://wired.jp/2021/01/08/new-media-studio-ouchhh/","line":124}],"metadata":{"title":"Mysterious Things are the Most Beautiful──the Public Experience Installations of “Ouchhh”, a Media Art Studio Based in Istanbul","source":"https://wired.jp/2021/01/08/new-media-studio-ouchhh-en/","author":["[[Rie Noguchi]]"],"published":"2021-01-08","created":"2026-05-19","description":"“Ouchhh” is a cutting-edge, media art studio based in Istanbul Turkey that has attracted attention from around the world, that has released a series of works in collaboration with NASA, CERN, and others. Its AI-based works, developed from the concept that \"the roots of art and science are mysterious”, have been exhibited in major cities around the world. This is WIRED Japan’s interview with Ferdi Alici, the founder of Ouchhh, about its activities.","tags":["#clippings"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},"smart_blocks:raw/Mysterious Things are the Most Beautiful──the Public Experience Installations of “Ouchhh”, a Media Art Studio Based in Istanbul.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"last_embed":{"hash":"11nvedw","at":1779224661311},"embeddings":{"TaylorAI/bge-micro-v2":{"vec":[-0.00971932,-0.03481106,0.03512378,0.00193521,0.03070757,-0.0282392,-0.02112902,-0.01285753,0.00970732,-0.0042561,-0.00107383,-0.0493821,0.01894137,0.02779467,0.00737857,-0.00749491,0.03600969,-0.00762779,-0.08678561,-0.02193613,0.12809718,0.00718789,0.02715094,-0.07142048,-0.02109891,0.02566252,-0.02253507,-0.02231715,-0.0256857,-0.15004581,-0.04145283,-0.0160248,0.11746603,-0.02315492,0.03448288,0.01747633,-0.03589154,-0.04396969,-0.07087277,0.05602525,0.02751975,0.00204501,-0.07655909,-0.08244556,0.01554587,-0.02574174,0.0190195,-0.06617836,-0.01737217,-0.05746397,0.06379361,0.00244024,-0.00341168,0.01052706,0.08216989,0.00070819,0.04718097,0.01964537,0.029711,-0.00936352,0.051